131   4193              ; send: 16 bytes from HL down the screen, from the VRAM address in DE (the
132   4193              ; write bit and the table in D); C: the line of the first. Inside a cell the
133   4193              ; next line is the next byte (chapter 22): the bytes go in runs, one for each
134   4193              ; cell, and between runs the address moves to line 0 of the cell below.
